<title>USA: ComEd Quad Cities Ill. nuke hits 100 pct.</title>
<headline>ComEd Quad Cities Ill. nuke hits 100 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co's 789 megawatt (MW) Quad Cities nuclear unit 1 has returned to full power, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Friday.</p>
<p>The Cordova, Ill., unit was reduced to about half power last weekend for repairs to a steam seal system.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with an identical generating capacity, is also operating at 100 percent power.</p>
<p>Commonwealth Edison is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
